# {{ project_slug }}

> Generated by [HarnessForge](https://github.com/EpisodeYu/HarnessForge) — an agent harness you own. **No agent-framework lock-in** (no LangChain / LangGraph / ADK), and no runtime dependency on HarnessForge.

This is a thin, framework-free agent harness: a native function-calling loop, a
tool registry, an OpenAI-compatible LLM client, JSONL tracing, and a CLI. Read
it, edit it, delete what you don't need — it's yours.

## Quickstart

```bash
uv sync                              # uv installs the right Python + an isolated venv
uv run {{ project_slug }} run --mock "hello"   # offline smoke run, no API key needed
```

To talk to a real model, add your key and drop `--mock`:

```bash
cp .env.example .env                 # then edit .env with your real key(s)
uv run {{ project_slug }} run "What time is it in UTC?"
```

Prefer pip? A `requirements.txt` is provided as a fallback:

```bash
python -m venv .venv && . .venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt && pip install -e .
{{ project_slug }} run --mock "hello"
```

## Run in Docker (host-independent)

```bash
docker build -t {{ project_slug }} .
docker run --rm {{ project_slug }}                          # mock one step
docker run --rm -e OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-... {{ project_slug }} run "hello"
```

## Loop paradigms

This harness can run a turn in different **paradigms**, picked per turn:

{% for p in paradigms %}{% if p == "agent" %}- **agent** (default) — full Think → Act → Observe tool-calling loop; may call any allowlisted tool and self-corrects on tool errors.
{% elif p == "plan" %}- **plan** — read-only: investigates with low-risk tools and outputs a step-by-step plan; never makes changes.
{% elif p == "ask" %}- **ask** — read-only: answers questions, may use low-risk tools, never makes changes.
{% endif %}{% endfor %}
```bash
uv run {{ project_slug }} run --mode plan "add a retry to the API client"
```

The selectable roster + default live in `config.yaml` under `paradigms:` (a
runtime knob). Each paradigm is a small, self-contained file under
`src/{{ project_slug }}/harness/paradigms/` — read it, edit it, or add your own
(see [`AGENTS.md`](./AGENTS.md)). It's a plain name→function registry, not a
framework.
